  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Using the normal approximation to the binomial distribution, approximate the probability that a fair spinner with five regions: red, green, orange, white, and blue, lands on green or white more than $25$ but less than $35$ times out of $80$ spins. Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0582\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0570\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0559\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0708\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0694\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0681\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0854\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0838\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0823\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6808\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6844\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6879\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EA